; claude: a small JavaScript (plan_tiny_firefox.md, notes_javascript.md):
; Js_lexer (the text to tokens), Js_ast (the tree), Js_parse (statements
; by recursive descent, expressions by Pratt -- and why not yacc),
; Js_value (values, objects, the conversions), Js_eval (the tree
; walked: scopes, closures, this, the errors) and Js_builtins (console,
; Math, strings' and arrays' methods). The language only: what a script can
; touch outside itself is its host's, a record of functions, so
; TinyFirefox gives it a page and a test gives it nothing.
;
; Pure OCaml, no Playground (libs/languages/README.md); the modules
; are Js_ because the libraries are unwrapped and js_of_ocaml's own
; module is Js. A private library, installed as part of elm_playground.
(library
 (name javascript)
 (package elm_playground)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries random) ; Lehmer, Math.random's seeded numbers
)
